      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HELLIVIT (1) is at his best when allowed to make his own rules in front, and he did just that here 3 weeks ago when making all the running to score by more than 2 lengths. This is tougher, but on his best day, he is hard to beat. REAL VALENTIA (3) is a well-travelled veteran who slides down into a very competitive level for this. He gets a nice draw upgrade and can bounce straight back into the money here. Each way. VERBOSITY (2) has looked a lot better in this last couple of starts, and dropping back to 1100m from 1400m will help him. Include in all top 3 combos in the small field. TELLEZ (4) overdid it in front when taking his hook last time out, and he understandably faded in the run home. He is much better placed over 1200m, and he can make amends. TANGO STEPZ (5) is a durable veteran mare who normally comes to hand quickly, and the small field suits her. Keep safe.",
